+// src/ik2/ik2_serve.hpp - maya-ik2 --serve --parallel N: the multi-request loop (serve_loop) and its host bookkeeping,
+// over a model side that ik2_main.cu's serve_multi gives it (the GPU work), so that tests check the loop with no GPU and
+// no model: tests/ik2_serve_test.cpp its parts, tests/ik2_serve_fake.cpp the whole protocol over a stand-in model.
+//   * Lines: stdin's lines in the order they came (a reader thread only reads; what a line means is the loop's).
+//   * parse_gen: a GEN / GENI line, checked before it may take a slot - its rid, a whole max_new of 0 or more, every
+//     token id in the vocabulary, the prompt and max_new within the context (compared without overflow).
+//   * Control: the lines taken one at a time, in that order: requests queued, STOP <rid> and STOP.  STOP stops every
+//     request whose line came before it - decoding, its prompt being read, or waiting for a slot - and none that came
+//     after; a stopped waiting request is retired at once (its DONE), slot or no slot.  A STOP for no live request is
+//     dropped: nothing is kept for later, so nothing piles up.
+//   * Book: the slots' kept tokens and the snapshot pool's index - which slot a request takes and from where, what
+//     that drops, and what a prompt stopped while it was read leaves: an empty slot.
+//   * pick_top / pick_next: a row's next token.  A greedy row takes the raw logits' argmax (before the softcap) in
+//     every step, sampled rows beside it or not.
+#pragma once
+
+#include "../mm3/mm3_slots.hpp"
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cerrno>
+#include <climits>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <condition_variable>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdio>
